  "title": "Intercommunal trauma centre for psychosocial assistance in response to floods in Schleiden, Germany",
  "summary": "An intercommunal trauma centre provides free short- to long-term psychosocial support to citizens and emergency service workers in the Schleiden region, Germany to reduce mental health impacts of heavy rain and flood events. Heavy rains and floods hit North Rhine-Westphalia and Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany in July 2021, affecting thousands of people in the region and beyond. With climate change, extreme events such as heavy rains and resulting floods are expected to increase in frequency and severity.",
